abstract: >-
  Benchmark of six regression families (Explainable Boosting Machine, Elastic Net,
  Random Forest, XGBoost, Support Vector Regression and a fastai neural network),
  with ordinary least squares as a linear reference, used as per-project surrogates of
  stochastic project duration. Activity durations of 400 PSPLIB projects are simulated
  by Monte Carlo from an earned value control point; hyperparameters are selected on
  40 projects and the retained configurations are evaluated on 360 held-out projects.
  The repository contains the project instances, simulation outputs, selection and
  evaluation results, and the statistical analyses. Version 2.0 adds a confirmatory study on
  320 new PSPLIB networks under a frozen protocol: critical-set competition as a structural
  explanation of surrogate accuracy, fidelity of local explanations, and a simulated
  intervention-decision test.
